From 1ac957bbbffec625fb7df5c80f821785c3ba3f61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:32:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] moe cache: RAM tier for the cold experts of an mmap
 master (GGML_MOE_RAM_TIER_MIB)

Without it, the cold reads and fills of an mmap table come from the registered file alias.  Here every sparse table,
once sized, also gets an exclusive pinned (and mlocked) copy of exactly the experts its arena does not hold, in the
arena's compact layout, and the file pages are dropped once every table of a master has its tier.  An admission swaps
arena <-> tier on the compute stream (victim D2H into the spare tier slot, expert H2D out of its tier slot, both as
copy kernels); the freed slot is reused only after its copy completed.  The cold read in mul_mat_vec_q_moe gets a
per-expert source address (cold_ptrs: a tier slot, or a file alias address with the low bit set for the host
geometry), and the prefill fills read the tier.  On for every sparse table or for none: over GGML_MOE_RAM_TIER_MIB
(default 60 % of RAM), on an allocation or swap failure, a re-size, a stand-down, an arena shrink / release or a slab
eviction every tier is dropped and the cold reads go back to the registered alias (the behaviour of the previous
commit).  GGML_MOE_RAM_TIER_MIB=0: off.
